KNOWN TRAPS FOR THESE TICKETS:
- MOCK3-1 (age-65 fare boundary): the rule documented in src/fares.ts is "65 AND OVER", so the cutoff must be inclusive (`age >= 65`, not `age > 65`). The existing specs never test age 65 exactly (they test 70), so green tests do not prove the boundary. Require a spec at the boundary value itself (65) and one just below it (64); absence of a boundary-value test is at least a minor issue. Also confirm the child concession cutoff (age < 13) was not disturbed.
- MOCK3-2 (final stop omitted): formatStops iterates `i < stops.length - 1`, dropping the last stop. The fix must include the final stop in the rendered string and still handle an empty stops array (totalMinutes already guards this; formatStops must not regress on it). Judge by whether the output ends with the final stop, not merely by whether it contains the '->' separator or early stops.

REVIEW RULES:
- Map every issue to at least one acceptance criterion from __STORY_ACS__; if none apply, it is not a finding.
- Before reporting a blocker, reproduce it with the commands above and cite the failing output in the issue description.
- Approve only when every acceptance criterion is met AND boundary/edge specs as described above exist and pass.

